[38;5;231m⏺[39m The repo is a single static [38;5;153mindex.html[39m with an empty [38;5;153m<main>[39m — one commit, "initial: empty tasks page". There are no
  tasks, no users, no persistence, and no server.

  That matters for scoping. "Notify users when tasks they care about change" presupposes four things that don't exist
  here yet:

  - [1mTasks[0m — a data model and somewhere to store them
  - [1mUsers[0m — identity, so "who cares about what" is even expressible
  - [1mChange events[0m — something that detects and records a change worth announcing
  - [1mDelivery[0m — how a notification actually reaches a person

  Notifications are the last of those, not the first. I'm not going to design a notification subsystem on top of three
  subsystems that need to be designed too — that's how you get a spec whose assumptions are all invented.

  So before I ask anything else: I want to know whether this repo is really the whole app.
